KORTEX PAST EXAMINATION PAPERS
ENGINEERING - Thermodynamics (Year 2023)

Q1. What is the maximum theoretical efficiency of a Carnot heat engine operating between 600 K and 300 K?
  (A) 25%
  (B) 50%
  (C) 75%
  (D) 100%
  Answer: B - Carnot efficiency = 1 - (T_cold / T_hot) = 1 - (300 / 600) = 0.50 (50%).


